# This harness's own signing seed. gantry template init generates it at mode
# 0600 and it is the one piece of real key material in here: whoever holds it
# can sign events as this harness, so a signature stops proving which run wrote
# an event. It is ignored rather than allowlisted in a scanner, because a
# scanner exemption would say the opposite of what is true about this file.
#
# If it is committed anyway, the fix is not to delete the file: generate a new
# harness key, update its public half in config/actor-keys.json and the key id
# in profile_requirements.attestation in config/policy.json, and remove the old
# seed from history.
config/actor-key.seed

# Ledgers are append-only records of runs, not source.
ledger/
